36,2,1,talk,May,,"The diary proves Saturdays are triple Tuesdays. Plus, tracking every run took an hour weekly. That’s the real cost I’m fighting.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The receipts show two of us bought most fuel, while one barely drove. The mechanic warns short city runs wear the car faster.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,I found the poison. Checking figures made everyone feel accused. Other groups failed because asking for favors felt like begging. We need a system that removes the ask.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, your fuel data matches mine. Two people did most driving, one barely any. Plus, fixed costs hit 280,000 yen. We need a fair split based on actual use, not guesses.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, your hour of tracking is exactly the friction I face. I found the car often empty or dirty, and our weekly trips keep collapsing.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, exactly. That hour is pure admin. If we pick a system that needs constant checking, I’m out. We need something that runs itself.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, I hear your exhaustion. Yet the mechanic’s warning is clear: short, cold runs damage the car. We must balance your time with the vehicle’s health.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@May, I agree. If the system forces us to ask favors, it fails. We need a way to use it without the awkwardness.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May, I agree. If tracking takes an hour, it’s too much. But we need to know who drives to split the 280,000 yen fairly.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Takumi, your point about favors is key. My weekly trips collapse because we rely on asking. I need a system that guarantees my slot without the awkwardness.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Takumi, agreed. No more begging. But @Kenji, if we don’t track, how do we split the 280k? I refuse to subsidize your heavy weekends.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, a fair split requires knowing the true burden. The car’s health and the uneven fuel use demand we look beyond simple time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@May, I get the money worry. But if we start checking figures, we become enemies. We need a system where nobody has to ask or audit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@May, I hear you. But without tracking, we’re just guessing again. I need the real figures to split the 280k fairly, not just by who complains loudest.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, I need my weekly slot guaranteed. If the car is dirty or empty, my routine breaks. I need a system that protects my time, not just the money.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Kenji, I refuse to be the unpaid accountant. If the system demands constant auditing, I’m out. We need something that runs itself without the drama.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, fairness is not merely arithmetic; it is the health of our bond. We must choose a path that respects both the ledger and the spirit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Kenji, I get the need for numbers, but checking them destroyed us before. We need a system that doesn’t force us to audit each other.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I get the fear. But I need the baseline to stop guessing. Let’s find a way to split the 280k without turning into accountants.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
